  "raw": " human-driven mass extinction, the giant meteor shower that hit Earth last year and the rising ocean waters. But it turns out that more than a hundred worlds with advanced life forms also collapsed over the same time period—and now scientists can explain exactly why.\n\nNASA’s Stratospheric Aerosol and Gas Experiment (SAGE) mission launched in 2006 to study planet-scale chemical dynamics. The experiment sent thousands of tiny particles floating into the stratosphere to measure changes in the composition of the stratosphere. They were carried into the stratosphere by winds of oxygen and hydrogen gas, but they also included trace amount of carbon dioxide. Over time, SAGE tracked how quickly this carbon dioxide changed chemistry and interacted with the other gases. Since the particles were tiny, the rate measurement was only a few parts per billion (ppb) in terms of the amount of gases they were carrying. However, over a 100-year period, the chemical reactions were measured and the rate changed from",
